        <div class="cfedContentLimiter">
            <div class="row content-row">
                <div class="col">
                    

    <div class="cfedContent">
        
        <div class="cfedContent__body">
            
                                    


        </div>
    </div>


    <div class="cfedContent">
        
        <div class="cfedContent__body">
            
                <div class="cfedContent__text"><div class="header2023">
<div class="header2023-text-wrapper">
    <div class="header2023-text-block">
<h1 class="header2023-page">Events</h1>
    </div>
</div>
</div>



</div>
                        


        </div>
    </div>


    <div class="cfedContent">
        
        <div class="cfedContent__body">
            
                <div class="cfedContent__text"><div class="pageSection2023">
<p class="cyanLargeText">The Federal Reserve Bank of Chicago hosts a range of events each year. They include banking conferences, community development and economic mobility panels, convenings around issues affecting the Seventh District, industry-specific talks, and more. All of our events center on the bank’s mission to advance a strong economy, promote a trusted financial system, and serve the public good. Here you can find recordings and transcripts of past events and discover upcoming ones. </p>
</div></div>
                        


        </div>
    </div>


    <div class="cfedContent">
        
        <div class="cfedContent__body">
            
                <div class="cfedContent__text"><div class="cfedContent__text pageSection2023">
    <div class="cyan-section-header">Upcoming Events</div>

  
    <div class="cyan-publication-containerA">
        <!--<p>There are no upcoming events scheduled at this time.</p>-->
        <!--Event Listings-->

 
       <div class="cfedEvent__wrapper">
            <div class="cfedEvent__wrapper-itemLeft">
                <h2><a href="/events/2026/community-bankers-symposium">20th Annual Community Bankers Symposium</a></h2>
                <div class="cyan-publication-event-date">September 10, 2026</div>
<p style="display:block;">The 20th Annual Community Bankers Symposium, <i>Community Banking in the New Normal</i>, will be hosted by the Federal Reserve Bank of Chicago, the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation, the Office of the Comptroller of the Currency and the Conference of State Bank Supervisors on Thursday, Sept. 10, 2026, for an in-person event with a remote attendance option.</p>
                <!-- <button type="button" class="ctaButton2023"><a href=" https://cvent.me/NA9YOR">Register Now</a></button>-->
            </div>
            <div class="cfedEvent__wrapper-itemRight">
                <img src="/-/media/images/events/2026/community-bankers-symposium/community-bankers-symposium_web1.png?sc_lang=en&amp;hash=8B4E4D6619583189991A7DA88A4B6548" alt="Community Bankers Symposium event banner" />
            </div>
        </div>



      <div class="cfedEvent__wrapper">
            <div class="cfedEvent__wrapper-itemLeft">
                <h2><a href="/events/2026/housing-affordability-community-development-summit">Housing Affordability 2026: A Community Development Summit</a></h2>
                <div class="cyan-publication-event-date">September 22-23, 2026</div>
<p style="display:block;">On Tuesday and Wednesday, September 22 and 23, 2026, the Federal Reserve Bank of Chicago will host Housing Affordability 2026: A Community Development Summit, an event for community leaders and Federal Reserve community development experts from across the United States to share insights, analysis, and tools related to this vital topic.</p>
                 <button type="button" class="ctaButton2023"><a href="https://cvent.me/0rB9Be">Register Now</a></button>
            </div>
            <div class="cfedEvent__wrapper-itemRight">
                <img src="/-/media/images/events/2026/housing-affordability-2026/housing-affordability-2026_web1.png?sc_lang=en&amp;hash=E7591563E25EC3757374644DB9A09E70" alt="Housing Affordability event banner" />
            </div>
        </div>


         <div class="cfedEvent__wrapper">
            <div class="cfedEvent__wrapper-itemLeft">
                <h2><a href="/events/2026/why-consumers-economists-see-different-economies">Why Consumers and Economists See Different Economies</a></h2>
                <div class="cyan-publication-event-date">September 30, 2026</div>
                <p>The Federal Reserve Bank of Chicago, in collaboration with NORC at the University of Chicago, will bring together leading data experts alongside consumers, small business owners, and nonprofit leaders to explore what’s driving consumer sentiment, how it has shifted over time, and which additional measures of economic health can deepen our understanding of lived economic conditions.</p>
                 <button type="button" class="ctaButton2023"><a href="https://cvent.me/O35MzR">Register Now</a></button>
            </div>
            <div class="cfedEvent__wrapper-itemRight">
                <img src="/-/media/images/events/2026/why-consumers-economists/why-consumers-economists_web1.png?sc_lang=en&amp;hash=51A9C1F942AB00FA1C051398B549414C" alt="Why Consumers and Economists See Different Economies event banner" />
            </div>
        </div>

   <div class="cfedEvent__wrapper">
            <div class="cfedEvent__wrapper-itemLeft">
                <h2><a href="/events/2026/midwest-agriculture-conference">Midwest Agriculture Conference</a></h2>
                <div class="cyan-publication-event-date">October 16, 2026</div>
                <p>On October 16, 2026, the Federal Reserve Bank of Chicago will hold its annual Midwest Agriculture Conference, a hybrid event featuring experts from academia, industry, and policy institutions.</p>
                <button type="button" class="ctaButton2023"><a href="https://cvent.me/adzEmV">Register Now</a></button>
            </div>
            <div class="cfedEvent__wrapper-itemRight">
                <img src="/-/media/images/events/2026/midwest-agriculture-conference/midwest-agriculture-conference_web1.png?sc_lang=en&amp;hash=898886E3A72A3CB2E376F901009DF5C3" alt="Midwest Agriculture Conference event banner" />
            </div>
        </div>
    </div></div></div>
                        


        </div>
    </div>


    <div class="cfedContent">
        
        <div class="cfedContent__body">
            
                <div class="cfedContent__text">
<div class="pageSection2023">

<div class="calloutBox2023">
        <h3>Remarks From the President</h3>
<p>The president and CEO of the Chicago Fed speaks regularly at events hosted by the Chicago Fed as well as other organizations. Here you can find his speaking schedule, read his formal remarks, and view videos of past speeches.</p>

<button type="button" class="ctaButton2023"><a href="/utilities/about-us/office-of-the-president/office-of-the-president-speaking">Speaking Engagements</a>
</button>

</div></div></div>
                        


        </div>
    </div>


    <div class="cfedContent">
        
        <div class="cfedContent__body">
            
                <div class="cfedContent__text"><div class="pageSection2023">
        <div class="cyan-section-header">Past Events</div>
        <div class="cyanPublicationNote">
            <h5>Watch replays, access slides, and read transcripts.</h5>
</div>


<div class="cyan-publication">
<h2><a href="/events/2026/workers-ai-impact">Workers and AI Impact: How Do Past Forecasts Compare to the Present Reality?</a></h2>
<p class="cyan-publication-event-date">August 25, 2026</p>
<p>The Chicago Fed’s Economic Mobility Project hosted Workers and AI Impact: How Do Past Forecasts Compare to the Present Reality?, a virtual event during which Kristen Broady, director of the Economic Mobility Project, presented recent research examining how employment and wages changed from 2019 to 2024 across occupations with varying levels of automation risk and AI applicability. The presentation was followed by a panel discussion moderated by Jim Lecinski with Antwi Akom, Edward Colgate, and Scott Ransom.</p>
</div>


<div class="cyan-publication">
<h2><a href="/events/2026/affordable-housing-chicago-faith-organizations">Creating Affordable Housing: The Efforts of Chicago Faith-based Organizations</a></h2>
<p class="cyan-publication-event-date">June 30, 2026</p>
<p>On June 30, 2026, the Chicago Federal Reserve Bank organized a discussion about how faith-based organizations are working to convert their real estate and Chicago’s vacant properties into appealing and affordable housing communities.</p>
</div>

<div class="cyan-publication">
<h2><a href="/events/2026/vanishing-tax-credits-shrinking-market-who-can-afford-rent">Vanishing Tax Credits and a Shrinking Market: Who Can Afford to Rent?</a></h2>
<p class="cyan-publication-event-date">May 26, 2026</p>
<p>On Tuesday, May 26, the Chicago Fed’s Economic Mobility Project hosted Vanishing Tax Credits and a Shrinking Market: Who Can Afford to Rent?, a virtual event focused on the Low-Income Housing Tax Credit.</p>
</div>


<div class="cyan-publication">
<h2><a href="/events/2026/fed-life-unlocked">Fed Life Unlocked</a></h2>
<p class="cyan-publication-event-date">April 17, 2026</p>
<p>On Friday, April 17, 2026, the Federal Reserve Bank of Chicago invited students interested in economic research to an exclusive career exploration event. </p>
</div>


<div class="cyan-publication">
<h2><a href="/events/2026/human-capital-time-low-real-rates">Human Capital in a Time of Low Real Rates</a></h2>
<p class="cyan-publication-event-date">March 31, 2026</p>
<p>On Tuesday, March 31, 2026, at 11:00 a.m. CT, the Chicago Fed’s Economic Mobility Project hosted a virtual event, Human Capital in a Time of Low Real Rates.</p>
</div>

<div class="cyan-publication">
<h2><a href="/events/2026/joint-conference-on-financial-crises">2026 Joint Conference on Financial Crises</a></h2>
<p class="cyan-publication-event-date">February 19, 2026</p>
<p>The inaugural Joint Conference on Financial Crises, hosted by the Federal Reserve Bank of Chicago and the Yale University Program on Financial Stability, took place Thursday, February 19, 2026.</p>
</div>

<div class="cyan-publication">
<h2><a href="/events/2026/ais">Amenities and Office Vacancy Rates: What Really Draws Workers Back to the Office?</a></h2>
<p class="cyan-publication-event-date">February 11, 2026</p>
<p>On Wednesday, February 11, 2026, the Chicago Fed’s Economic Mobility Project hosted the virtual event, Amenities and Office Vacancy Rates: What Really Draws Workers Back to the Office?</p>
</div>

<div class="cyan-publication">
<h2><a href="/events/2026/ais">32nd Annual Automotive Insights Symposium</a></h2>
<p class="cyan-publication-event-date">February 4-5, 2026</p>
<p>On February 4-5, 2026, the Federal Reserve Bank of Chicago, Detroit Branch hosted the 32nd Annual Automotive Insights Symposium.</p>
</div>

<div class="cyan-publication">
<h2><a href="/events/2025/economic-outlook-symposium">39th Annual Economic Outlook Symposium</a></h2>
<p class="cyan-publication-event-date">December 12, 2025</p>
<p>The Federal Reserve Bank of Chicago hosted the 2025 Economic Outlook Symposium on December 12 in Chicago, Illinois. </p>
</div>

<!--<div class="cyan-publication">
<h2><a href="/events/2025/financial-markets-group-fall-conference">Financial Markets Group Fall Conference</a></h2>
<p class="cyan-publication-event-date">November 19, 2025</p>
<p>The Financial Markets Group hosted its fall conference on Wednesday, November 19, 2025. </p>
</div>


<div class="cyan-publication">
<h2><a href="/events/2025/artificial-intelligence-office-factory">Artificial Intelligence in the Office and the Factory</a></h2>
<p class="cyan-publication-event-date">November 10, 2025</p>
<p>On Monday, November 10, 2025, at 11:00 am CT the Chicago Fed’s Economic Mobility Project hosted the virtual event, Artificial Intelligence in the Office and the Factory.</p>
</div>



<div class="cyan-publication">
<h2><a href="/events/2025/sixth-annual-exploring-career-pathways">Sixth Annual Exploring Career Pathways</a></h2>
<p class="cyan-publication-event-date">October 30, 2025</p>
<p>On October 30, 2025, the Federal Reserve Bank of Chicago hosted the Sixth Annual Exploring Career Pathways in Economics and Related Fields Conference.</p>
</div>


<div class="cyan-publication">
<h2><a href="/events/2025/third-party-service-provider-risks-economy-financial-system">Third-party Service Provider Risks in the Economy and Financial System</a></h2>
<p class="cyan-publication-event-date">October 16, 2025</p>
<p>This workshop presented by the Federal Reserve Bank of Dallas, brought together researchers, regulators and practitioners to explore how vulnerabilities related to third-party service providers can best be identified, monitored and mitigated.</p>
</div>



<div class="cyan-publication">
<h2><a href="/events/2025/community-bankers-symposium">19th Annual Community Bankers Symposium</a></h2>
<p class="cyan-publication-event-date">October 10, 2025</p>
<p>The 19th annual Community Bankers Symposium, Community Banking: Charting the Course, was held October 10, 2025, at the Federal Reserve Bank of Chicago.</p>
</div>


<div class="cyan-publication">
<h2><a href="/events/2025/midwest-agriculture-conference">Midwest Agriculture Conference</a></h2>
<p class="cyan-publication-event-date">September 30, 2025</p>
<p>On September 30, 2025, the Federal Reserve Bank of Chicago held a hybrid event featuring experts from academia, industry, and policy institutions that explored the evolving global trade environment and its impacts on Midwest agriculture.</p>
</div>

<div class="cyan-publication">
<h2><a href="/events/2025/resilient-tax-structures-economy">Taxing Times, Smarter Strategies: Resilient Tax Structures for a Changing Economy</a></h2>
<p class="cyan-publication-event-date">September 3, 2025</p>
<p>The Civic Federation and the Federal Reserve Bank of Chicago hosted Taxing Times, Smarter Strategies: Resilient Tax Structures for a Changing Economy on Wednesday, September 3, 2025 at the Federal Reserve Bank of Chicago.</p>
</div>




<div class="cyan-publication">
<h2><a href="/events/2025/zoning-strategies-and-tools-to-unlock-housing-supply-across-the-midwest">Zoning Strategies and Tools to Unlock Housing Supply Across the Midwest</a></h2>
<p class="cyan-publication-event-date">August 27, 2025</p>
<p>On Wednesday, August 27, from 11:00 am to 12:45 pm CT a virtual event featured local experts and practitioners who discussed zoning strategies and tools that are helping their Midwest communities assess their housing needs and address housing supply challenges. </p>
</div>


<div class="cyan-publication">
<h2><a href="/events/2025/building-for-affordability">Building for Affordability: Exploring Housing Supply Strategies in Chicago</a></h2>
<p class="cyan-publication-event-date">May 21, 2025</p>
<p>The Chicago Federal Reserve Bank held a webinar exploring housing supply strategies in Chicago on Wednesday, May 21, 2025, from 11:30-1:00 pm CT. </p>
</div>

<div class="cyan-publication">
<h2><a href="/events/2025/disaster-risk-and-the-new-shape-of-credit">Stormy Weather: Disaster Risk and the New Shape of Credit</a></h2>
<p class="cyan-publication-event-date">July 15, 2025</p>
<p>On Tuesday, July 15, 2025, the Chicago Fed&rsquo;s Economic Mobility Project held a virtual event, Stormy Weather: Disaster Risk and the New Shape of Credit, with a panel of experts who discussed how weather-related disaster risk impacts access to mortgage loans and business loans in the U.S. </p>
</div>



<div class="cyan-publication">
<h2><a href="/events/2025/child-rearing-local-amenities-urban-migration-market">Labor, Leisure, and Life Choices: How Child-Rearing and Local Amenities Impact Urban Migration</a></h2>
<p class="cyan-publication-event-date">July 10, 2025</p>
<p>On Thursday, July 10, 2025, at 11:00 am CT, the Economic Mobility Project of the Federal Reserve Bank of Chicago hosted a virtual discussion on the intersections of skill development, geographic mobility, and urban living.</p>
</div>-->






    
        <a class="gradientButton2023-long" href="/events/past-events">
            All Past Events
        </a>
    
    </div></div>
                        


        </div>
    </div>


